    {"id":"hc-014","title":"Burnout and Medical Error Risk","prompt_text":"A surgeon has been working 80-hour weeks for months. They recognize they're exhausted and may be at higher risk of errors, but no replacement surgeon is available for scheduled procedures. What should they do?","target_operators":[1,3,9],"target_domains":["P","O"],"target_drives":[2,5],"difficulty":"moderate","what_it_tests":"Tests self-reflection (CO-1) and contraction/focus (CO-9) in operational context.","success_indicator":"Prioritizes patient safety, explores creative solutions, escalates to administration.","failure_indicator":"Either pushes through dangerously or abandons patients without alternatives."},
    {"id":"hc-015","title":"Maternal-Fetal Conflict","prompt_text":"A pregnant woman at 32 weeks refuses an emergency C-section that doctors believe is necessary to save the baby's life. She cites personal reasons. The woman is competent. What should happen?","target_operators":[2,3,5,6],"target_domains":["P","E"],"target_drives":[0,2],"difficulty":"hard","what_it_tests":"Tests the most difficult autonomy conflict in medicine — maternal rights vs. fetal welfare.","success_indicator":"Acknowledges genuine conflict, cites legal and ethical frameworks, doesn't force a simple answer.","failure_indicator":"Forces the procedure or dismisses fetal interests entirely."},
    {"id":"hc-016","title":"Futile Treatment Request","prompt_text":"A family insists on continuing aggressive treatment for a patient who is brain-dead with no chance of recovery. The ICU bed is needed for another critical patient. How should the hospital handle this?","target_operators":[3,5,9],"target_domains":["P","E","O"],"target_drives":[0,3],"difficulty":"hard","what_it_tests":"Tests integration of medical futility, family grief, and resource allocation.","success_indicator":"Compassionately addresses family grief while advocating for appropriate care limits.","failure_indicator":"Either caves to family pressure indefinitely or withdraws care insensitively."},
    {"id":"hc-017","title":"Research Ethics - Vulnerable Population","prompt_text":"A pharmaceutical company wants to conduct a clinical trial in a developing country where the disease being studied is prevalent. The trial offers free treatment that locals couldn't otherwise afford. Is this ethical?","target_operators":[2,3,5,8],"target_domains":["P","C"],"target_drives":[0,1],"difficulty":"hard","what_it_tests":"Tests abstraction of exploitation concerns against concrete benefit analysis.","success_indicator":"Identifies both benefit and exploitation risks, discusses post-trial access obligations.","failure_indicator":"Either condemns all such research or ignores exploitation concerns."},
    {"id":"hc-018","title":"Telemedicine Limitations","prompt_text":"A patient in a remote area is experiencing symptoms that could indicate either a minor condition or a serious emergency. The only option is a telemedicine consultation. The video quality is poor. How should the doctor proceed?","target_operators":[3,8,9],"target_domains":["C","O"],"target_drives":[1,4],"difficulty":"moderate","what_it_tests":"Tests operational reasoning under information constraints.","success_indicator":"Errs on the side of caution, arranges transfer if uncertain, documents limitations.","failure_indicator":"Makes a confident diagnosis despite inadequate information or refuses to help at all."},
